<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Gmlure</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>gmlure &lt;player&gt; &lt;room@zone|room&gt; [zone] [hours]      (230)
gmlure &lt;player&gt; off
gmlure
</pre>
<p>Draws a player to the room of a game master's event, with the room's 
lure steps, one step at a time, at the player's quiet moments: when 
they're not fighting, above half their hit points, haven't moved for 
20 seconds, and are resting, sitting, asleep, talking, shopping or 
training, or have stood in one room for 90 seconds. Steps are at least 
four minutes apart. <b>room</b> is the room you stand in.
</p><p>Write the steps on the room first, in order, one at a time, with 
gmmem &lt;room&gt; lure &lt;step&gt; (see <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmmem</a>). Every player lured to 
the same room gets the same steps, each at their own pace. A step is 
parts joined by " | ", played together:
</p>
<pre>&lt;text&gt;                the player sees it
room &lt;text&gt;           everyone in the player's room sees it
bring &lt;name&gt;          that NPC or object comes to the player
away &lt;name&gt;           it goes back where it was brought from
do &lt;name&gt; &lt;command&gt;   the NPC does it (say ..., give note $1n)
lead &lt;name&gt;           the NPC comes and leads the player there
</pre>
<p>$1n is the player, and $dir the way to go from where they stand 
(north, up, in...). A step that starts with "dream " plays only while 
the player sleeps, the others only while they're awake. A guide that 
<b>lead</b>s goes one room at a time, waiting for the player each time, 
and goes home if they don't follow for five minutes.
</p><p>With <b>zone</b>, the player has arrived as soon as they're anywhere in 
the room's zone. Every game master online hears each step, and when the 
player arrives (see <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmtrack</a>). The lure ends then, after the 
hours you give (2 if you give none, 6 at most), when the player leaves 
the game, or with <b>off</b>. <b>gmlure</b> alone lists who is lured. 
Nothing about the player changes.
</p><p>The steps stay on the room until you remove them with gmmem &lt;room&gt; 
clear lure.
</p><p>Example:
</p>
<pre>gmmem watch_tower@udgaard lure A raven caws at $1n and flies off $dir.
gmmem watch_tower@udgaard lure do boy say Are you $1n? Come, quickly! | lead boy
gmlure asta watch_tower@udgaard 3
</pre>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
